# Lecture content (Learn courses)

## Writing

- The lecture (`bai-N.md`) must stand alone: approachable, engaging, every
  concept fully explained. Never defer an explanation to the question bank
  ("xem Câu 9").
- `bai-N-them.md` (quiz, guide, "Câu hỏi phản biện") is an optional advanced
  layer. Questions may go deeper but must not introduce concepts the lecture
  skipped.

## Source fidelity

- `bai-N.original.txt` is the word-for-word source the seed validates against.
  If you change lecture wording, regenerate the matching `.original.txt` (the
  `>` subtitle line under the H1 is excluded), then run
  `npx tsx scripts/seed-<course>-course.ts --dry-run` and confirm
  `matchPercent` is 100.

## Publishing to production

- Seed scripts create a course once and skip it if it exists. They never update
  production content.
- Edit live content in Learn Studio (`/my-space/courses/<slug>/studio`) or
  through the admin API with an admin session:
  `PATCH /api/admin/learn/sections/[id]`, `POST /api/admin/learn/lessons/[id]/sections`,
  `PUT /api/admin/learn/courses/[id]/outline`. Save a manual revision
  (`POST /api/admin/learn/sections/[id]/revisions`) before changing a live
  section; autosave keeps at most one snapshot per 10 minutes.
- Production may differ from local files (Studio edits). Read the live section
  first and patch the difference instead of overwriting it.
- Replacing content can delete learner progress. Confirm with the user before a
  replace or delete on a published course.
- Images referenced from lectures must exist in `public/learn/<course>/` and be
  deployed before the text that uses them; otherwise remove the image lines.
